11. SMART SUGGESTION ENGINES (pure functions, deterministic per seed, run client-side)
====================================================================================================

Shared UI component: <SuggestionStrip title items onApply onRefresh loading emptyText />  [MUST]
  - Horizontal scroll with scroll-snap, 8 px gap, edge fade, keyboard arrow navigation, each card is a button (role="button", clear label).
  - Header row: strip title (14/600) + optional context chip (e.g. a colour dot and "Dark, cool blue") + REFRESH icon at the far right.
  - Skeleton cards while computing (> 80 ms). Empty state: "No safe ideas for this background. Try another background or tap refresh."
  - Applying a card = one undoable change; snackbar "Applied . Undo".

REFRESH ICON  <RefreshButton onClick busy />  [MUST]
  - Icon only (Lucide RefreshCw, 20 px, stroke 1.75, muted colour), 44 x 44 hit area, tooltip/title "New ideas", aria-label "Show new ideas".
  - On tap: refreshCount++, icon rotates 360 deg in 500 ms (reduced motion: no rotation, brief opacity pulse), button disabled for 600 ms,
    new cards fade in (stagger 30 ms), light haptic (navigator.vibrate(10)) where available.
  - aria-live="polite" announcement: "8 new ideas" (buttons), "6 new combinations" (fonts), "6 new layouts" (layout).
  - The previous set is kept in a 3-step in-memory history so a long-press (or the overflow menu "Previous ideas") can go back.
  - Never return a combination already shown in the last 40 (ring buffer in sessionStorage), except if the pool is exhausted.

11.1 BUTTON COLOUR SUGGESTIONS  suggestButtons(bgProfile, vibe, current, locks, seed, seen) -> 8 ButtonSet
  ButtonSet = { id, recipe, name, fill, text, border, borderWidth, surface?, shape?, subtle?: boolean, why: string, scores }
  Recipes (formulas in OKLCH relative to the background profile; always gamut-reduce, always run the T-rules of 8.4):
   R1 "Contrast Ink"   light/mid-light bg: fill = oklch(0.18, min(0.03, 0.35*C), h) ; dark/mid-dark bg: fill = oklch(0.97, min(0.012, C), h).
                        text = bestText(fill) ; border = fill ; borderWidth 0. Baseline: prefer text/fill >= 7:1.
   R2 "Tonal Soft"     [SOFT] fill = bg L -0.07 (light) / +0.07 (dark), C = max(C, 0.02)*1.1 ; text = oklch(0.26 or 0.93, 0.02, h) ; border = fill L -+0.06 ; borderWidth 1.
   R3 "Accent Pop"     hue = h + 180 (+-20 seeded jitter) for chromatic bg ; seeded hue for neutral bg ; L = 0.78 (dark bg) or 0.52 (light bg) ; C = 0.17 gamut-reduced ;
                        text = bestText ; border = fill. If T3 fails (e.g. orange page + teal fill = 1.9:1) push L toward an extreme in 0.02 steps or add a 2 px ink border; else discard.
   R4 "Analogous Glow" hue = h +-28 ; L as R3 ; C = 0.11 ; border = fill L +0.08 ; add glow shadow 0 8px 24px fill@35 %.
   R5 "Outline Clean"  fill transparent ; text = oklch(0.2 or 0.95, 0.02, h) ; border = text ; borderWidth 1.5 -> 2 ; requires T2 >= 7:1 worst-case.
   R6 "Glass"          surface glass ; light bg: fill rgba(255,255,255,0.55), text ink ; dark bg: fill rgba(255,255,255,0.12), text paper ; border rgba(255,255,255,0.32) ;
                        evaluate contrast on the blended fill over the darkest AND lightest sample ; only if C1 allows.
   R7 "Inverse Duo"    fill = oklch(clamp(1 - L, 0.12, 0.92), min(C, 0.06), h) ; text = the page colour adjusted to pass 7:1 ; border = text, 2 px.
   R8 "Triad Bold"     hue = h +120 or h -120 (seeded) ; L/C as R3.
   R9 "Vibe Accent"    fill = the active vibe accent (adjusted by 0.02 L steps until T1/T3 pass) ; text = bestText.
   R10 "Gold Foil"     only if tone dark, or warm hue with meanL < 0.6 ; surface metallic gold ; text #0A0A09 ; border #E7C873.
   R11 "Neon Edge"     only if tone dark ; fill = bg L +0.03 (C <= 0.06) ; text = border = oklch(0.86, 0.17, seeded hue 150..330) ; surface neon-glow.
   R12 "Wildcard"      seeded: random recipe parameters inside the same constraints (a hue anywhere on the wheel, L within the tone-table band, C <= cap).
  Pipeline [MUST]:
   1) Generate 3 variants per recipe with seeded jitter (hue +-12 deg, L +-0.03, C x0.85..1.10)  -> ~36 candidates.
   2) Drop candidates failing STRICT (SOFT recipes use the SOFT exceptions). Drop candidates incompatible with C1-C11 for their surface.
   3) Respect locks: locked fields keep their value; recompute the others to stay valid (fill locked -> bestText + border; text locked -> search fills that pass T1;
      border locked -> keep and validate T3). If a locked combination cannot be made valid, show it with a "Low contrast" tag instead of hiding.
   4) Score = 0.45*contrastScore + 0.25*harmonyScore + 0.15*vibeAffinity + 0.15*novelty.
        contrastScore = min(1, (textContrast-4.5)/(10-4.5)) averaged with min(1, (affordance-3)/(8-3)).
        harmonyScore = 1 for exact analogous/complement/triad/split hue relations (+-6 deg), falling to 0 at +-30 deg; neutral sets score 0.8.
        vibeAffinity = 1 - min(1, deltaE(fill, vibe.fill or vibe.accent) / 0.35).     novelty = min(1, deltaE to nearest seen set / 0.12).
   5) Select 8: at most 2 per recipe, pairwise fill deltaE >= 0.09 or different surface, at least one of {R1,R5}, at least one of {R3,R4,R8,R9}, SOFT sets only after slot 3.
      First load (refreshCount = 0): slot 1 is always the best R1 so the user sees the safest option first.
   6) Name each set (recipe name + optional hue word, e.g. "Accent Pop . Violet") and write the "why" line ("Deep ink on a light page. Easy to read.").
  Card (148 x 96 px): a real mini button 120 x 40 drawn with the set's exact fill/text/border and the CURRENT shape and surface; under it name (13/600), a contrast chip
   ("AAA 12.1", "AA 5.4"), three tiny colour dots, and a "Subtle" tag when SOFT. Tap = apply. Long-press / "..." = "Colours only" or "Colours + style".
  Applying sets fill, text, border, borderWidth, and (only for R4, R6, R10, R11) the surface; shape and size are never changed by an idea. Applied values are stored as
   overrides with no lock; the user can then fine-tune in the colour rows.

11.2 FONT SUGGESTIONS  suggestFonts(bgProfile, vibe, current, locks, seed, seen, isPro) -> 6 FontCombo
  FontCombo = { id, name?, mood, nameFont:{family,weight,tracking}, bioFont:{...}, buttonFont:{...}, locked: boolean (needs Pro), scores }
  Mood inference (weights, then take the top 3 moods):
    vibe collection + tags (0.4) ; background tone/chroma/complexity (0.4) ; current button surface (0.2).
    dark + neutral -> modern, techy, luxury | light + neutral -> calm, modern, editorial | light + warm -> warm, editorial, friendly, organic |
    meanC >= 0.10 -> bold, playful, friendly | type glass/aurora/neon or surface neon/glass -> futuristic, techy | paper/grain textures -> editorial, classic |
    surface offset-3d/sticker -> playful, bold | surface metallic/underline -> luxury.
  Candidates: the curated pairings of 10.4 (18) plus 30 generated combinations.
  Generation rules:
    NAME font: role N, moods overlap >= 1, weight 600-800 (display fonts 400-900 per availability), tracking: tight (-0.02em) for large display, wide (+0.04em) when case = upper.
    BIO font: role B, legibility >= 0.8, xHeight >= 0.48, weight 400 (on dark backgrounds allow 400-500, never below 400), never script/condensed/pixel.
    BUTTON font: role T, either the bio family at weight 500-600 or a UI sans/mono with legibility >= 0.75; uppercase only if the family supports it well (sans, mono, roman caps).
    Category contrast: NAME category must differ from BIO category (serif display + sans, sans display + serif text, mono + sans, rounded + serif ...), unless both come from the same superfamily.
    Limit: <= 3 distinct families overall. Dark backgrounds: bump weights +50..100 (max 700) and tracking +0.01em to counter halation.
  Score = 0.40*moodMatch + 0.25*categoryContrast + 0.20*legibility + 0.15*novelty ; subtract 0.20 for Pro-locked combos when the user is not Pro.
  Select 6: 3 curated + 3 generated, at most 2 locked (Pro) combos for free users, no two with the same NAME family. First load: slot 1 = curated pairing that best matches the vibe.
  Card (188 x 132): three real lines (display name, 40-char bio snippet, mini button label) + mood tag + lock badge. Tap applies all three roles (source = "suggestion").
  Locked roles (font.name / font.bio / font.button) keep their value and the engine only fills the other roles.

11.3 LAYOUT SUGGESTIONS  suggestLayouts(bgProfile, vibe, buttons, current, locks, seed, seen) -> 6 LayoutIdea
  Pipeline: take the 12 recipes of 10.7 -> drop any that violate C1-C11 for the current background/buttons -> score = 0.40*moodOverlap(vibe, recipe) + 0.30*backgroundFit +
  0.15*novelty + 0.15*consistency(current surface if locked) -> add 2 seeded MUTATIONS of the top recipes (spacing +-1 step, width +-1 step, avatar frame swapped within its mood) ->
  select 6 with distinct header or link layout. Applying an idea sets only layout tokens (header, avatar, linkLayout, spacing, width, entrance, social style) and, when the
  recipe names a surface/size/motion and those are NOT locked, the button surface/size/motion too (ask nothing, show Undo).
  Card (140 x 120): tiny wireframe from the tokens + recipe name + one-line tag ("Glass . Airy").

