13. API, VALIDATION AND PRO GATING
====================================================================================================

  Endpoints (adapt to the existing API style; Next.js route handlers or server actions are fine):
    GET   /api/appearance                       -> { appearance, resolved, entitlements, warnings }
    PATCH /api/appearance                       -> JSON merge-patch of Appearance; returns the new appearance + warnings; coalesces history snapshots within 2 s
    POST  /api/appearance/undo | /redo          -> moves through the last 20 snapshots
    POST  /api/appearance/themes                -> save current as a theme ; GET list ; POST apply ; PATCH rename ; DELETE
    POST  /api/appearance/background-image      -> returns a signed upload URL ; a server job resizes, strips EXIF, stores dominant colours + 8x8 luminance grid
  Validation (zod or the existing validator): hex regex /^#([0-9a-fA-F]{3}|[0-9a-fA-F]{6}|[0-9a-fA-F]{8})$/ normalised to 6/8 digits upper-case; numbers clamped to their ranges;
    enum values checked; font ids must exist in the catalogue and weights must be offered by the family; max 3 families; max 4 gradient stops; image size/type checked.
  Pro gating (server-side, reuse the existing entitlement helper): Pro vibes, Pro backgrounds (all presets tagged PRO, image, animated), Pro fonts, Animate toggle,
    themes beyond the free limit. On violation return HTTP 402 with { code: "PRO_REQUIRED", fields: ["background.preset", ...] } and DO NOT persist the offending fields
    (persist the rest). The client then opens the upgrade sheet. If the plan lapses, Pro-only values stay stored but the renderer falls back to the nearest free equivalent.
  Concurrency: send updated_at/ETag; on conflict return 409 with the latest appearance; the client merges field-by-field and keeps the user's newest edits.
  Rate limit 60 requests/min per user; log validation failures (no PII).

